{% set products = guest.product_get_list %}
<div class="accordion-item">
    <h3 class="accordion-header">
        {# This step only renders when no product has been chosen, and it was
           the ONLY step in the accordion that never received `show`. Every
           other one opens conditionally (#order when a product is set,
           #register / #checkout when ?checkout=1), so landing on /order with
           no product left every panel shut: a page of headings with nothing
           to act on and no way forward. Signing in from there looked like the
           login had failed, because the page genuinely could not advance.
           It is the first step of the flow, so it opens by default. #}
        {# Only open this when there is genuinely nothing else to resume. A
           signed-in visitor with a domain already in the cart who lands on
           plain /order was being sent back to "Select Product" — the first
           step of a purchase they are already halfway through. #}
        {% set kzd_cart = guest.cart_get %}
        {% set kzd_cart_count = kzd_cart.items is defined ? kzd_cart.items|length : 0 %}
        {# The catalogue is a detour, not the entry point: it opens only when
           the visitor picks it from this header. The domain step owns the
           "nothing selected yet" state instead (see
           mod_orderbutton_product_configuration.html.twig), which is both the
           flow this site is built around and what the step indicator above
           already claims is active.

           The one exception is a store with no domain product at all, where
           there would be nothing for the domain step to default to. Without
           this fallback that state has no open panel -- the dead end that was
           reported twice. The condition is the exact inverse of the one that
           defaults the domain step, so between them every state is claimed by
           exactly one panel, never zero and never two (two is not benign: the
           accordion is data-bs-parent bound and silently keeps only the
           first). #}
        {% set kzd_has_domain_product = guest.product_category_get_list.list|reduce(
            (carry, category) => carry|merge(category.products|filter(p => p.type == 'domain')), [])|length > 0 %}
        {% set kzd_open_products = not request.product and kzd_cart_count == 0 and not kzd_has_domain_product %}
        <button class="accordion-button{% if not kzd_open_products %} collapsed{% endif %}" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#products" aria-expanded="{{ kzd_open_products ? 'true' : 'false' }}" aria-controls="products">
            <svg class="icon me-2"><use href="#apps" /></svg>
            <span>{{ 'Select Product'|trans }}</span>&nbsp;<span class="badge bg-info">{{ products.list|length }} {{ 'Items'|trans }}</span>
        </button>
    </h3>
    {# `and not request.checkout` is load-bearing: with a domain already in
       the cart the URL is /order?checkout=1 and carries no product param, so
       keying only off `request.product` opened this panel there too. The
       accordion is data-bs-parent bound and shows one panel at a time, so
       this step won the slot ahead of #register / #checkout and the cart
       flow dead-ended on "Select Product" instead of reaching payment. #}
    <div id="products" class="accordion-collapse collapse{% if kzd_open_products %} show{% endif %}" data-bs-parent="#orderManager">
        <div class="accordion-body">
            {% for i, category in guest.product_category_get_list.list %}
                <h4 {% if i > 0 %} class="mt-3" {% endif %}>{{ category.title }}</h4>
                <span>{{ (category.description ?? '')|markdown_to_html }}</span>
                <div class="kzd-order-product-grid">
                    {% for i, product in category.products|sort((a, b) => a.priority <=> b.priority) %}
                        {% set product_icon = product.type == 'domain' ? 'search' : (product.type == 'hosting' and 'email' in product.slug ? 'mail' : (product.type == 'hosting' ? 'layout-grid' : 'apps')) %}
                        <a class="kzd-order-product-card" href="{{ 'order'|url(query: { 'product': product.id, 'show_custom_form_values': request.show_custom_form_values }) }}">
                            <span class="kzd-order-product-icon"><svg class="icon"><use href="#{{ product_icon }}" /></svg></span>
                            <span class="kzd-order-product-title">{{ product.title }}</span>
                            <svg class="icon kzd-order-product-arrow"><use href="#arrow-right" /></svg>
                        </a>
                    {% endfor %}
                </div>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
